  "body": "## What happens\n\n`crates/app/tests/plunge_depth_tab.rs` `the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_names_its_tab_window_dives` fails on main since `afadbf4eb` (merge of PR #3847). It fails on the Linux post-merge runs and on both Windows checks:\n\n    assertion `left == right` failed: three tab window dives named\n    (the count is not read from the log yet; 0 is the expected value after #3866)\n\nThe post-merge run of `4b5cb0d2d` (PR #3866) is green. Each run from `afadbf4eb` is red.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe two PRs merged cleanly in git but disagree in behaviour:\n\n- PR #3847 (#3679) added the verifier note `PlungeTooDeep` and this test. The test reads `examples/catalog/2d/contour-tabs` and expects three dives of 6 mm on the last level against a 2 mm stepdown.\n- PR #3866 (#3678), merged one minute before, pecks a contour dive deeper than one stepdown below the cut floor. The three tab-window dives are now pecked, so the verifier correctly names no dive.\n\nThe toolpath is correct. The test expectation is out of date.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The test pins the new behaviour on the `contour-tabs` case: no `PlungeTooDeep` note, and each later tab window on the last level descends in steps of at most the 2 mm stepdown.\n- The `PlungeTooDeep` note stays pinned on a case that still has a deep dive (a fixture that #3866 does not peck, for example an entry that is not a contour dive), so the #3847 check keeps its coverage.\n- `plunge_depth_tab` is green on main.",
